00:49:37.741 --> 00:49:38.642
because he was like,

00:49:38.642 --> 00:49:39.977
Dude, how can you read this?

00:49:39.977 --> 00:49:41.945
This is like
the most important thing

00:49:41.945 --> 00:49:43.313
that we have to do
to be able

00:49:43.313 --> 00:49:45.248
to plan our business
moving forward.

00:49:45.248 --> 00:49:46.483
So I remember the next day

00:49:46.483 --> 00:49:47.684
I spent the entire day

00:49:47.684 --> 00:49:49.786
and we were just reading
this book

00:49:49.786 --> 00:49:50.721
cover to cover.

00:49:50.721 --> 00:49:52.389
And I would say
what happened

00:49:52.389 --> 00:49:53.657
there is

00:49:53.657 --> 00:49:55.525
that was kind
of the turning point

00:49:55.525 --> 00:49:57.861
of us

00:49:59.062 --> 00:49:59.463
getting

00:49:59.463 --> 00:50:00.797
more proactive
about the business.

00:50:00.797 --> 00:50:02.332
And I think
in a lot of ways,

00:50:02.332 --> 00:50:04.668
Austin taking on the
responsibilities

00:50:04.668 --> 00:50:06.436
of the CEO of the company

00:50:06.436 --> 00:50:08.572
because I think in
a lot of ways by following

00:50:08.572 --> 00:50:09.840
that process, it

00:50:09.840 --> 00:50:12.642
it forces you to

00:50:12.642 --> 00:50:12.943
think

00:50:12.943 --> 00:50:14.611
strategically about
what is the plan

00:50:14.611 --> 00:50:15.746
for the business
moving forward.

00:50:15.746 --> 00:50:17.614
Forces you to think about
who is your leadership team

00:50:17.614 --> 00:50:18.682
and who are you hiring into.

00:50:18.682 --> 00:50:20.384
Your leadership team forces
you to set

00:50:20.384 --> 00:50:21.651
quarterly goals, run

00:50:21.651 --> 00:50:23.286
leadership meetings, etc.

00:50:23.286 --> 00:50:24.388
And I think after

00:50:24.388 --> 00:50:26.656
that point, there was

00:50:26.656 --> 00:50:28.759
I kind of knew it in

00:50:29.192 --> 00:50:30.961
like my heart of hearts

00:50:30.961 --> 00:50:33.296
that what I was spending
my time on

00:50:33.597 --> 00:50:37.100
was largely the stuff that
I was still energized by.

00:50:37.100 --> 00:50:38.402
So like new products,

00:50:38.402 --> 00:50:39.603
like our new podcast,

00:50:39.603 --> 00:50:41.304
our new newsletters, new

00:50:41.304 --> 00:50:43.407
things
like our education business.

00:50:43.673 --> 00:50:45.509
But what I wasn't
spending my time on

00:50:45.509 --> 00:50:46.943
or not actually energized by

00:50:46.943 --> 00:50:48.512
was in a lot of ways

00:50:48.512 --> 00:50:50.580
what the job was of the CEO.

00:50:50.580 --> 00:50:51.982
As you go into company
building

00:50:51.982 --> 00:50:53.350
and not product building.

00:50:53.350 --> 00:50:55.519
And I would say it, it
largely

00:50:55.519 --> 00:50:57.421
led to ultimately Austin

00:50:57.421 --> 00:50:59.523
having to have
very difficult conversations

00:50:59.523 --> 00:51:01.324
about him
moving from the CEO

00:51:01.324 --> 00:51:03.193
role into the CEO
role, moving me,

00:51:03.193 --> 00:51:04.728
moving from the CEO
to the chairman

00:51:04.728 --> 00:51:07.197
role,
I think largely because

00:51:07.197 --> 00:51:08.732
I didn't kind of acknowledge

00:51:08.732 --> 00:51:10.467
this truth or all earlier

00:51:12.135 --> 00:51:14.304
and because

00:51:14.304 --> 00:51:15.305
I think I had always kind

00:51:15.305 --> 00:51:16.640
of had this perception

00:51:16.640 --> 00:51:17.774
in building a business

00:51:17.774 --> 00:51:19.876
that you have to be
the CEO forever,

00:51:19.876 --> 00:51:21.144
because a lot of who

00:51:21.144 --> 00:51:22.946
my role models were for
such a long time,

00:51:22.946 --> 00:51:24.648
whether it's Bezos or Gates,

00:51:24.648 --> 00:51:26.383
like any of these people,

00:51:26.416 --> 00:51:27.250
they start the business

00:51:27.250 --> 00:51:28.718
and they run it
until it goes public.

00:51:28.718 --> 00:51:30.921
Basically, they're the
captain of the ship forever.

00:51:30.921 --> 00:51:33.990
And I think that kind of ego
held me

00:51:34.124 --> 00:51:35.325
from actually doing

00:51:35.325 --> 00:51:36.626
what I think
was right, actually,

00:51:36.626 --> 00:51:37.961
for everyone, for me,

00:51:37.961 --> 00:51:41.031
for Austin,
for the business.

00:51:41.131 --> 00:51:42.599
So I know
we're running up here

00:51:42.599 --> 00:51:43.800
against the end of time.

00:51:43.800 --> 00:51:45.702
I have one question
that I really do

00:51:45.702 --> 00:51:48.004
want to ask you
as both on a personal level

00:51:48.004 --> 00:51:49.573
that I think will resonate
with a lot of folks

00:51:49.573 --> 00:51:51.208
out there and founders,

00:51:51.208 --> 00:51:52.742
builders, etc..

00:51:52.742 --> 00:51:54.611
You ended up selling
at least

00:51:54.611 --> 00:51:56.046
a portion of morning brew.

00:51:56.046 --> 00:51:58.215
I know
you guys are still owners

00:51:58.715 --> 00:52:00.717
to Business Insider in 2020.

00:52:01.952 --> 00:52:04.054
Yes, October of 2020.

00:52:04.087 --> 00:52:04.821
Okay.

00:52:04.888 --> 00:52:05.789
In that transaction,

00:52:05.789 --> 00:52:08.125
both of you guys
made a lot of money.

00:52:08.125 --> 00:52:10.260
You had presumably been
paying yourself salaries

00:52:10.260 --> 00:52:12.062
for a while
and had been doing well

00:52:12.062 --> 00:52:14.131
because the business
was doing well and you owned

00:52:15.132 --> 00:52:16.233
close to 100%, 90

00:52:16.233 --> 00:52:18.702
plus percent of the business
at the time.

00:52:18.702 --> 00:52:20.604
You made a lot of money
in this transaction.

00:52:20.604 --> 00:52:21.705
Are you happier?

00:52:21.705 --> 00:52:24.641
Do you feel like,
you know, creating

00:52:24.674 --> 00:52:27.277
tens of millions of dollars
of personal wealth has made

00:52:27.277 --> 00:52:28.812
you a happier person

00:52:28.812 --> 00:52:30.347
on a daily basis?

00:52:30.347 --> 00:52:31.014
Yeah, I can start.

00:52:31.014 --> 00:52:34.284
So I was
I was reading a book

00:52:34.284 --> 00:52:36.153
or an excerpt from a book

00:52:36.153 --> 00:52:37.487
that Will Smith wrote,

00:52:37.487 --> 00:52:38.788
and he had this quote
that I think

00:52:38.788 --> 00:52:40.624
it wasn't about money,
but I think it

00:52:40.624 --> 00:52:42.826
it translates so well.

00:52:42.826 --> 00:52:45.328
And the quote was about fame

00:52:45.662 --> 00:52:47.864
and it was getting something
to the effect

00:52:47.864 --> 00:52:50.433
of getting famous
is amazing.

00:52:50.433 --> 00:52:52.369
It's like absolutely
incredible.

00:52:52.369 --> 00:52:54.604
Being famous is cool.

00:52:54.604 --> 00:52:55.739
It's nice,

00:52:55.739 --> 00:52:57.874
but losing fame is horrible.

00:52:58.375 --> 00:53:00.944
And I think the same thing
is true about money, right?

00:53:01.111 --> 00:53:02.946
Am I happier? I think 100%.

00:53:02.946 --> 00:53:04.347
Like I think

00:53:04.347 --> 00:53:06.550
I am absolutely happier
because I have more money.

00:53:08.185 --> 00:53:08.985
And I think there's like

00:53:08.985 --> 00:53:10.620
that whole $70,000

00:53:10.620 --> 00:53:12.189
seller study

00:53:12.189 --> 00:53:13.456
that people are happier
saying,

00:53:13.456 --> 00:53:14.724
I've got $70,000.

00:53:14.724 --> 00:53:15.725
I don't think that's true.

00:53:15.725 --> 00:53:18.361
I think I am happier.

00:53:18.361 --> 00:53:20.330
But I think there are also

00:53:20.330 --> 00:53:22.499
a lot of things that

00:53:23.099 --> 00:53:25.202
make me not happy.

00:53:25.202 --> 00:53:25.535
Right.

00:53:25.535 --> 00:53:27.437
And so, like on the net,
I am happier.

00:53:27.437 --> 00:53:28.939
But there are also
tons of things

00:53:28.939 --> 00:53:30.373
like, for example,

00:53:30.373 --> 00:53:33.376
when you have money,
it's like

00:53:33.376 --> 00:53:35.845
the money is step
wise, right?

00:53:35.845 --> 00:53:37.180
And so making an incremental

00:53:37.180 --> 00:53:38.782
5% on net worth

00:53:38.782 --> 00:53:40.250
means nothing to me. Right?

00:53:40.250 --> 00:53:41.551
And so

00:53:41.952 --> 00:53:43.620
that motivation
just changes.

00:53:43.620 --> 00:53:43.887
Right?

00:53:43.887 --> 00:53:46.089
And the drive is
just different.

00:53:46.089 --> 00:53:46.456
Right?

00:53:46.456 --> 00:53:49.025
And so net net, I'm happier.

00:53:49.025 --> 00:53:51.061
But the risk reward

00:53:51.061 --> 00:53:53.296
profile of everything
just changes.

00:53:53.296 --> 00:53:55.732
It just complicates
everything

00:53:55.732 --> 00:53:57.267
and just makes things
more difficult.

00:53:57.267 --> 00:53:59.302
So I think I'm happier.

00:53:59.302 --> 00:54:00.503
But again, like

00:54:00.503 --> 00:54:01.671
I lose a dollar,
I'm like, Oh,

00:54:01.671 --> 00:54:02.973
that sucks, right?

00:54:02.973 --> 00:54:05.041
Know, one small thing is
I used to love to, like,

00:54:05.041 --> 00:54:07.344
go to a casino
casino and gamble,

00:54:07.711 --> 00:54:09.813
and now I'll probably never
gamble again in my life.

00:54:09.813 --> 00:54:11.581
Same way
I can't ever gamble.

00:54:11.581 --> 00:54:12.082
Yeah.

00:54:12.082 --> 00:54:13.617
And what's funny is when I.

00:54:14.551 --> 00:54:16.286
When I before I sold money,

00:54:16.286 --> 00:54:17.087
I would love nothing more

00:54:17.087 --> 00:54:18.321
than to go play three,

00:54:18.321 --> 00:54:19.456
3 hours of blackjack

00:54:19.456 --> 00:54:20.690
for a couple of hundred
bucks

00:54:20.690 --> 00:54:21.691
right now.

00:54:21.691 --> 00:54:24.160
Like I

00:54:24.160 --> 00:54:25.562
betting $300, like,

00:54:25.562 --> 00:54:27.330
isn't exciting to me,

00:54:27.330 --> 00:54:28.265
but I would never bet

00:54:28.265 --> 00:54:29.966
something that I hate
losing it.

00:54:29.966 --> 00:54:31.034
I hate it.

00:54:31.034 --> 00:54:32.202
And so it just like,

00:54:32.202 --> 00:54:33.069
you know, having money

00:54:33.069 --> 00:54:34.471
change my relationship
with money,

00:54:34.471 --> 00:54:36.273
it's made me happier,
but it just made it

00:54:36.273 --> 00:54:37.107
very awkward.
It's like that.

00:54:37.107 --> 00:54:38.875
I personally haven't
spent enough time

00:54:38.875 --> 00:54:40.644
thinking about
internalizing like.

00:54:40.644 --> 00:54:41.945
Like what makes me happy.

00:54:41.945 --> 00:54:43.246
Now I have a certain

00:54:43.246 --> 00:54:44.481
threshold of money.

00:54:44.481 --> 00:54:46.583
Alex Yeah, I would say

00:54:47.350 --> 00:54:48.985
one of the functions

00:54:48.985 --> 00:54:51.521
of moving into the chairman
role and going from

00:54:51.521 --> 00:54:52.922
spending a ton of time

00:54:52.922 --> 00:54:55.759
in the business
to less time in the business

00:54:55.759 --> 00:54:56.993
is it left me with time.

00:54:56.993 --> 00:54:58.261
So I spend probably

00:54:58.261 --> 00:54:59.462
too much time

00:54:59.462 --> 00:55:01.398
thinking about this and I

00:55:01.398 --> 00:55:03.500
would say a few things.

00:55:04.501 --> 00:55:06.636
I feel incredibly fortunate

00:55:06.636 --> 00:55:08.705
to be in the position
that I'm in

00:55:08.705 --> 00:55:10.740
because I would say
the thing

00:55:10.740 --> 00:55:12.375
that that kind of add one

00:55:12.375 --> 00:55:14.044
to the scoreboard for money

00:55:14.044 --> 00:55:16.980
is to not have to feel

00:55:17.714 --> 00:55:20.517
finding financial anxiety

00:55:20.517 --> 00:55:21.718
ever again in my life

00:55:21.718 --> 00:55:23.787
unless I royally fuck
something up

00:55:23.787 --> 00:55:27.023
is just an amazing blessing.

00:55:27.023 --> 00:55:29.025
I would say after our

00:55:29.025 --> 00:55:30.527
the deal,

00:55:30.794 --> 00:55:32.128
and especially

00:55:32.128 --> 00:55:33.496
after
moving out of the CEO role

00:55:33.496 --> 00:55:34.964
because like these are two
big moments.

00:55:34.964 --> 00:55:36.599
They happen relatively
close to each other.

00:55:36.599 --> 00:55:38.735
Deal was October of 2020

00:55:38.735 --> 00:55:39.502
moved out of the

00:55:39.502 --> 00:55:42.372
the role in April of 2021.

00:55:42.372 --> 00:55:43.273
My happiness actually

00:55:43.273 --> 00:55:45.008
went down a lot.

00:55:45.308 --> 00:55:47.610
And it went down because one

00:55:47.610 --> 00:55:48.645
I realized I,

00:55:48.645 --> 00:55:50.880
I had money anxiety in life

00:55:51.181 --> 00:55:53.216
actually not tied to my net
worth.

00:55:53.383 --> 00:55:55.552
Like I still have money
anxiety today,

00:55:55.552 --> 00:55:57.787
even though it isn't
necessarily rational.

00:55:57.787 --> 00:55:59.556
I think it's potentially
because we didn't

00:55:59.556 --> 00:56:00.790
talk about money growing up,

00:56:00.790 --> 00:56:02.392
potentially
to generational thing,

00:56:02.392 --> 00:56:04.027
a cultural thing,
I don't know.

00:56:04.027 --> 00:56:06.162
But so
I didn't have the crutch of

00:56:06.162 --> 00:56:07.597
like money

00:56:07.597 --> 00:56:09.332
going to remove my money
anxiety.

00:56:09.332 --> 00:56:10.700
So it's now
something I have to work on

00:56:10.700 --> 00:56:12.268
irrespective of it,

00:56:12.268 --> 00:56:13.536
I would say.

00:56:13.536 --> 00:56:15.038
The second thing is

00:56:15.038 --> 00:56:17.807
I was absolutely motivated

00:56:17.807 --> 00:56:18.775
